WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.800
The War in Ukraine has been raging for ten
months now.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.080
In the first days of the war, Russia made
rapid advances on three axes, threatening

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.420
to conquer Ukraine’s East, South and Center.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.380
Instead, the Russian army suffered a massive
defeat around Kyiv, then around Kharkiv, then

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.040
in the South-West, around Kherson.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.480
Russians are now down to controlling Crimea,
parts of the East, and a strip of land connecting

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.480
the two.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.080
They are on the defensive almost everywhere,
and have opted to conduct massive terror bombardments

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.710
of Ukrainian civilian infrastructure with
ballistic missiles.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.539
All in all, Russians seem to have become stuck,
with no victory in sight.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:29.539
Or have they?

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.079
Lately there has been more and more talk of
a second Russian offensive against Kyiv, and

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.900
Ukrainians seem to be struggling somewhat
with the defense of Bakhmut, a strategically

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.190
important city in the East.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.770
As winter approaches, what can we expect on
the short, mid and long term?

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.350
Will there be a second Battle of Kyiv?

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.350
Let’s take a look.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.410
The most important question to answer first
and foremost, is “What are current Russian

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.950
war goals in Ukraine?”

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.670
And the answer is: the exact same as before:
the conquering of Ukraine.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.660
Now you might think that’s absolutely ludicrous.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.260
After all those defeats and humiliations,
a hundred thousand casualties and currently

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.980
8480 visually confirmed heavy equipment losses,
does Putin still seriously intend on conquering

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:04.980
Ukraine?

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:05.980
Yes.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:07.430
That still remains the political goal of this
war for Russia.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.740
And the Russian leadership plans to achieve
this via, for example, bombing Ukrainian civilian

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.350
infrastructure with ballistic missiles --a
war crime--, to deprive Ukrainians of heat

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.340
and energy during winter, thus degrade the
morale of both the population and the troops.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.180
However, this plan doesn’t seem to be working.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.960
Though they have done significant damage to
Ukrainian energy facilities, most Russian

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.130
ballistic missiles are still getting shot
down.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.850
From their latest, massive barrage of 76 missiles,
60 were shot down by Ukrainian air defense,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.520
with some failing on their own before even
reaching Ukraine.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.119
Meanwhile, partner countries keep supplying
electric equipment and generators to help

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:39.990
keep the Ukrainian grid operational.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.369
And so far they’ve been successful.

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:45.310
In addition, at the time of making this video
it seems more and more likely that the US

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.659
will deliver its advanced Patriot air defense
systems to Ukraine, which would dull the edge

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:50.590
of Russian terror bombings even further.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:54.100
But ballistic missiles aimed at civilians
is not the only way Putin is trying to get

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.100
his way.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.240
As of the second half of December, 2022, rumors
are circulating about a new Russian offensive

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.240
against Kyiv.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.710
The commander of the Ukrainian military, General
Zaluzhnyi, was quoted saying he has “no

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.439
doubt they will have another go at Kyiv.”

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:09.599
The Institute for the Study of War assesses
such offensive to be “extraordinarily unlikely

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:10.599
to succeed”.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:14.100
However, so far such minor details haven’t
stopped Russians from trying.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.660
If Russians indeed decide to attack, they
would need to drag Belarus into the conflict,

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.450
which Putin seems to be attempting currently.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.120
In a very rare personal visit to Belarus,
Putin will no doubt try to pressure Lukashenko

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.349
into joining the invasion.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:26.530
However, for Lukashenko this is extremely
dangerous.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.920
If the Belarussian armed forced get chewed
up inside Ukraine, and there is a very good

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.670
chance they would, that would weaken Lukashenko’s
rule directly, since the only thing keeping

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.020
him in power is brute force at this point.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.450
The Belarussian military is in no shape for
an invasion.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.580
They have around fifty thousand military personnel,
with obsolete equipment.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.280
And they cannot throw everything at Ukraine
either, because then who will man the borders,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.069
who will keep the order in case people try
to overthrow Lukashenko again, and so on.

00:02:49.069 --> 00:02:51.520
And it’s not like Ukrainians would be caught
by surprise.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.739
Ever since beating the Russians out of the
north, they’ve established proper defenses

00:02:54.739 --> 00:02:56.159
along the Belarussian border.

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:59.800
If the fresh and somewhat prepared Russian
military couldn’t break the original defenses

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.720
that time, a worn-down Russian military with
rag-tag Belorussian support certainly won’t

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.500
break the improved defenses this time.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.530
Now let’s talk about the Ukrainian objectives.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.049
The long-term goal is of course the same:
remove Russian troops from the entire territory

00:03:11.049 --> 00:03:12.049
of Ukraine.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:15.379
The short-term goal is to keep the Russians
at bay in the East, and gain advantageous

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:17.830
positions everywhere via incremental progress.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.270
The mid-term goals are far more interesting
however.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.549
Ever since the Ukrainian victory and Russian
withdrawal in Kherson, there has not been

00:03:23.549 --> 00:03:25.390
any major breakthroughs along the frontlines.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:29.120
That was due to the Ukrainian mud season,
which makes large-scale maneuvers practically

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.120
impossible.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.950
However, that certain cold season is coming.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.439
In a few weeks the ground will freeze solid,
enabling maneuvers once again.

00:03:35.439 --> 00:03:38.810
And this is when I believe Ukraine will start
another large-scale offensive.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:39.810
But where?

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.959
In the South, the two armies are separated
by the massive Dnipro river.

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:46.439
Trying to attack through it would be incredibly
difficult, and Ukrainians would run into prepared

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:48.409
Russian defensive lines on the other side.

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:52.439
In the East, Ukrainians are holding the line
and grinding down frustrated Russian assaults,

00:03:52.439 --> 00:03:56.320
this is the Bakhmut area, and are making incremental
advances towards Kreminna and Svatove, in

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.329
order to cut a major supply line for Russian
troops in the area.

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:00.989
The frontlines are largely static there.

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:04.819
I personally doubt we’ll be seeing any major
offensives in that area in the near future,

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:06.189
but I could be wrong of course.

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:07.390
This leaves us with the Southeast.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.769
A large, flat, open area, north of which the
Ukrainian military has been massing for months,

00:04:11.769 --> 00:04:12.939
not coincidentally.

00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:16.420
This is the most likely area of a large-scale
Ukrainian offensive, which I believe we’ll

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.720
be seeing in the coming months.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.180
The main objective of the Winter Offensive
would be to take Tokmak and Melitopol, both

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.180
being major supply hubs, thus cutting Russian
forces in half.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.560
Geographically speaking.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.650
IF Ukrainians manage to pull it off, I’m
fairly certain that would be the beginning

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.510
of the end for the Russian invasion.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:31.710
And why is that?

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.540
Currently Russian troops south of Kherson
and in Crimea can be supplied via two routes.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.390
One through Melitopol, and the other through
Kerch.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.900
However, the Kerch bridge has been damaged,
and is out of commission for heavy military

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.030
echelons for at least half a year or so.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.729
Russians therefore have to resort to ferrying
supplies to Crimea, which is slow, ineffective,

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:47.729
and vulnerable.

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:50.830
If the Melitopol supply route would be cut,
the Kerch ferry would be struggling to supply

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:54.120
both the Russian invasion force AND the civilian
population of Crimea.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.940
At that point, Russia would find itself in
a situation like Kherson, only on a larger

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.940
scale.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.060
Where they have a whole lot of troops dug
in, connected by a crippled supply line, slowly

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.650
being ground down by Ukrainian strikes and
assaults.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.780
But this I believe is on the farther end of
the Ukrainian midterm goals.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.480
So where does all this put Russian mobilization
efforts?

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:14.259
Can Russia come out with a massive wave of
fresh troops to overwhelm Ukrainian defenders,

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:15.669
and achieve their war goals?

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:16.669
No.

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:19.289
The Soviet mobilization infrastructure is
largely gone.

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:21.970
What remains cannot cope with the sheer number
of new recruits.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.430
Beyond huge issues with training, including
the lack thereof, equipping those soldiers

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.500
is also either sub-par, or doesn’t happen.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.630
Many Russian mobilized have to buy their own
gear before heading into the combat zone.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:35.051
Such recruits can keep Ukrainian defenders
busy, but aren’t good for much else, such

00:05:35.051 --> 00:05:37.000
as complex combined arms maneuvers.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.600
I expect the lack of proper equipment will
become an especially severe problem during

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.600
the cold.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.460
Case in point, it’s not even the dead of
winter yet, but we’ve already seen Russian

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:47.660
troops affected by hypothermia due to lack
of winter gear.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.430
Soldiers also need to be fed more during the
cold, as the body burns more calories to keep

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:52.430
warm.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:55.600
With the current degraded, inefficient Russian
supply lines we’ll likely see food shortages

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.600
among Russian troops, further decreasing their
combat capabilities.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.680
If a well-supplied Ukrainian military attacks
then, things could get very ugly very fast

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.680
for the Russians.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.169
To sum up, winter is bound to be pretty hot
in Ukraine.

00:06:06.169 --> 00:06:10.169
The initiative remains firmly with Ukrainians,
and Putin or his general, Surovikin likely

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.520
won’t be able to change that, especially
with an ill-fated second assault on Kyiv.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.030
And if Ukrainians manage to take Melitopol
in the South and reach the sea, it would be

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:23.679
a game changer for this whole conflict, and
would mark the beginning of the end for the Russians.

